# Line endings: LF in the index AND in every working tree.
#
# Without this file, a Windows clone with the default `core.autocrlf=true`
# checks out CRLF while the index stays LF. That is normally invisible — but
# scripts/engine/challenger-logic.ts rewrites tiers.ts by regex and anchors on
# `;\n`, so a CRLF working tree makes replaceDeclaration() fail to find
# CHALLENGER_OVERRIDES and four tests in tests/challenger-edit.test.ts fail
# locally while CI (Linux, LF) stays green.
#
# That combination is worse than a plain broken test: it makes CLAUDE.md's
# "Run npm test before every push" unsatisfiable on Windows, which trains a
# contributor to push past a red suite. `eol=lf` keeps the checkout byte-identical
# to what the engine and CI actually run against.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries — never normalize, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.pdf binary
